<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern & conical tail spot-to-ring transition — MorphoEval overall 91.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) post-remediation evaluation of `1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py` (overall weighted score: 91.6 / 100, up +42.2 points from 49.4 / 100 in Pass 1). The remediated script integrates the nonlinear Thomas (1975) / Murray (1981) substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion PDE with zero-flux Neumann boundary conditions on both a planar 2D mammalian flank (via DCT-II IMEX, including Liu, Liaw & Maini 2006 two-stage spot-to-rosette maturation) and a curvilinear tapered conical cylinder (surface Laplace-Beltrami operator demonstrating the spot-to-ring transition at r_crit = 0.7527); verifies dual negative controls (d = 1.0 equal diffusion and K = 0.0 non-inhibitory Michaelis-Menten ablation); segments 164 markings on a SHA-256-locked Kruger Panthera pardus photograph; and backs its core identities with 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_003_mammalian_coat_markings.lean`. Overall 91.6/100 (faithfulness 91.0, reproducibility 93.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/mammalian_coat_markings_comparison.png: rendered output of 1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py at 8871db0, image/png, 736874 B, 2058×1297 px, artifact_sha256 7881aa275a9e22d0c7917148664b25bd6bfb18726a3ebb7a06eaa3c57fc85cbb (sha256 7881aa275a9e22d0c7917148664b25bd6bfb18726a3ebb7a06eaa3c57fc85cbb), spec_fingerprint b2430fa7555f7613c050c38a3e6a09c62deaaf4b43660495d846c209c0878084. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b2430fa7555f7613c050c38a3e6a09c62deaaf4b43660495d846c209c0878084; artifact_sha256: 7881aa275a9e22d0c7917148664b25bd6bfb18726a3ebb7a06eaa3c57fc85cbb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/mammalian_coat_markings_reference.json=24d56069831e0ee9..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/panthera_pardus_specimen.jpg=86533a5dcf9cfee6..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/scout_manifest.json=28eabc9cf247b03e...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mammalian-coat-markings-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend the two-stage rosette solver to full 3D finite-element surface meshes reconstructed from photogrammetric felid body scans." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.16e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
